Takes the keys of keyboards on iOS, iPadOS, Mac Catalyst, tvOS and visionOS from the presses of UIKit alone, which carry the keys of every source, such as a hardware keyboard, Full Keyboard Access, Voice Control, Switch Control, remote control and UI tests, while GameController reads only the keyboards of the hardware. So SDL reads no keyboard through GameController, turns every press into a key whether a keyboard is connected or not, and hands UIKit the presses whose key the app drops through its event filter, such as the Menu press of the Apple TV remote while the app leaves the back button to the system. Outside tvOS, whose focus hands the presses to the view, the view becomes the first responder once it is in a window, since UIKit hands the presses of a keyboard to the first responder. It also stops turning arrows and escape into key commands, and the swipes of the Apple TV remote into arrows, which the engine reads as the stick of the remote, and reads the Siri Remote that the joystick subsystem opens only where SDL builds that subsystem.

